==============================================================================
STAGE 5 -- the gradient through the subtraction
==============================================================================
  M = 64 construction evaluations, 32 evaluation points, 128 ANN parameters, float64
  basis rank 11/11
  criterion: central-difference agreement at or below 1e-06; latent rows exactly 0.0; the detached control must be WORSE than 1e-04

--- T1  autograd against an independent central difference (THE CRITERION) ---
  gradient norm: autograd 1.345535e+04, central difference 1.345535e+04
  RELATIVE 2-NORM DIFFERENCE = 1.8122e-09   MET (<= 1e-06)
  worst per-parameter relative difference = 3.8812e-04

--- T2  the additional-state columns are untouched, EXACTLY ---
  ANN columns [6, 7]: max abs subtraction = 0.0e+00, exactly zero = True

--- T3  THE DETACHED CONTROL, which must FAIL ---
  differentiated through     norm(F' dG~/deta) = 6.7069e-14
  DETACHED (the control)     norm(F' dG~/deta) = 5.8173e+01
  no projection at all       norm(F' dG/deta)  = 5.8173e+01

  ratio detached to unprojected: 1.000000   (1.0 means detaching buys exactly nothing)
  ratio through to unprojected : 1.1529e-15
  the control FAILS as required: True
  Detaching leaves the forward output identical and destroys the gradient property.
  This is why differentiating through the coefficient is not optional.

--- T4  the identity dG~/deta = (I - P) dG/deta ---
  four random parameter directions, relative difference between dG~/deta and
  (I - P) dG/deta: 1.051e-10, 2.801e-10, 6.518e-11, 6.423e-11
  (the floor here is the central-difference floor, near 1e-8, not autograd round-off)

--- T5  no gradient reaches the physical parameters through the basis ---
  d loss / d free_params = None
  The basis is built under no_grad at a detached expansion point and held for the
  epoch, so the physical parameters receive nothing through it. This is the ONE
  deliberate approximation in the gradient and it is verified here, not asserted.
  (the physical block still receives gradient through the ROLLOUT in a real model;
   this block is evaluated pointwise, so there is no rollout path to carry it)

--- T6  the latent path: what the FROZEN reference set does to d a / d eta_lat ---
  Proposition 7.1: with a baseline-only reference set the latent-path parameters get
  EXACTLY 0.000000e+00 sensitivity, because the latent-to-physical map is multiplied by
  zero where x_a = 0. The handoff expects candidate (a) to dissolve this, on the ground
  that rollout-drawn evaluation points carry nonzero x_a already. Measured below, that
  expectation holds for the VALUE of the coefficient and FAILS for its GRADIENT, and
  the reason is the freeze rather than the point set.

  (a) the GRADIENT, with the reference set FROZEN, which is the shipped design:
    construction evaluations                            latent-path     all params
    prescribed points, x_a scale 1.0                   0.000000e+00   8.933448e+08
    rollout 1 step, x_a from the network               0.000000e+00   6.264043e+07
    rollout 2 steps, x_a from the network              0.000000e+00   6.000253e+06
    rollout 2 steps, x_a FORCED to zero                0.000000e+00   6.624056e+06
  Exactly zero in EVERY row, the rollout rows included. A frozen point set is data:
  the latent output rows write ANN columns 6 and 7 only, the coefficient is fitted from
  the PHYSICAL columns, and with the points detached there is no remaining path.

  (b) the same with the reference points left ATTACHED, as the DIAGNOSTIC that
      isolates the freeze as the cause (this is NOT the shipped design):
    construction evaluations                            latent-path     all params
    rollout 1 step, attached                           5.487669e+05   6.769074e+07
    rollout 2 steps, attached                          7.356420e+04   6.630395e+06
    rollout 2 steps, attached, x_a forced to zero      0.000000e+00   7.204934e+06

  (c) the VALUE of the coefficient DOES depend on the latent content of the points:
    norm(a with x_a from the network - a with x_a forced to zero) / norm(a) = 1.5658e-01
    so the rollout-drawn points are not cosmetic; they change what is subtracted.

  READING. The handoff expected candidate (a) to dissolve the latent blindness. Half
  of that holds: the coefficient VALUE depends on the latent content of the reference
  points, by the amount in (c). The other half does not: d a / d eta_lat is EXACTLY
  zero under the shipped design, and (b) shows why -- it is the FREEZE, not the choice
  of points. And the freeze is not negotiable: the derivation rules out fitting the
  coefficient along the live trajectory precisely because the correction at step k
  would then depend on the learned writes at later steps, i.e. on the future.
  Stated carefully, because it is easy to overstate. The latent WRITE g_a is
  deliberately NOT orthogonalized and that is correct: the baseline defines no
  additional-state update, so the basis has zero rows there and there is nothing to be
  orthogonal TO. The physical write DEPENDENCE on the additional states IS projected,
  because the subtraction is evaluated at the actual rollout point with x_a included.
  What is exactly zero is narrower than either: only the sensitivity of the FITTED
  COEFFICIENT to the latent-path weights, the coefficient being fitted once per pass
  from a frozen snapshot. The projection is still applied in full at every point.
  So the limitation is real but small, and it does not change the design: the
  alternative is ruled out on causality.

